language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Fixed-charge production planning: shirts, shorts and pants share labour and cloth capacities, and each product can only be made on its machine after the machine is rented, at a fixed cost.
given num_products : int(1..)
given num_machines : int(1..)
$ product[p,1] is the profit per unit of product p and product[p,2] is the 0-based index of its machine
given product : matrix indexed by [int(1..num_products), int(1..2)] of int(0..)
given renting_cost : matrix indexed by [int(1..num_machines)] of int(0..)
$ use[p,k] is the amount of resource k (1 labour, 2 cloth) used per unit of product p
given use : matrix indexed by [int(1..num_products), int(1..2)] of int(0..)
given capacity : matrix indexed by [int(1..2)] of int(0..)
given max_production : int(0..)

find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..num_products)] of int(0..max_production)
$ y[m] is 1 when machine m is rented
find y : matrix indexed by [int(1..num_machines)] of int(0..1)
find z : int(-100000000..100000000)

maximising z
such that
$ a product can only be produced if its machine is rented (production is bounded by the maximum when the machine is rented, and zero otherwise)
forAll p : int(1..num_products) . (x[p] <= max_production * y[product[p,2]+1]),
$ the labour and cloth used by all products must stay within the labour and cloth capacity
forAll k : int(1..2) . ((sum p : int(1..num_products) . use[p,k] * x[p]) <= capacity[k]),
$ the profit is the profit from the products minus the cost of renting the machines
z = ((sum p : int(1..num_products) . product[p,1] * x[p]) - (sum m : int(1..num_machines) . renting_cost[m] * y[m]))
